{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.trace_interfaceLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.trace_interfaceLetter","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture.lean#L61-L69","doc":"Under a linear trace `t` with `t 1 = 1` and `t σ = z`, the letter's trace is the\nmixture of the two crossing traces, `(1 − e) z + e (z − h) = z − e h` — the corpus's bond\nfactor `z_D + d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.interfaceLetter_eq_mix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.interfaceLetter_eq_mix","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture.lean#L54-L59","doc":"**The interface letter is the `e`-mixture of the crossing and its inverse.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.mul_sub_smul_one_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.mul_sub_smul_one_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture.lean#L44-L52","doc":"**Under the Hecke relation `σ² = h σ + 1`, `σ − h·1` is a two-sided inverse of `σ`.**\nThis is the identification `σ⁻¹ = σ − h·1` the corpus writes as `T_i⁻¹ = T_i − A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.interfaceLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceLetter.interfaceLetter","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/InterfaceLetterCrossingMixture.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The interface letter `σ + d·1`, written through its inverse-crossing weight\n`e = −d/h`: `σ − (e h)·1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}